00:15:24.955 --> 00:15:26.076
I'd been out with a girlfriend.

00:15:26.456 --> 00:15:29.758
He wasn't happy with me going out so I didn't even bother going to bed,

00:15:29.778 --> 00:15:31.019
I just went and laid on the couch.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:37.764
And about three o'clock in the morning I was woken by him dragging me off the couch by my throat.

00:15:39.596 --> 00:15:44.098
And he nearly choked me to the point where I nearly blanked out.

00:15:46.239 --> 00:15:48.080
That was the point where I said,

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:49.260
enough.

00:15:53.683 --> 00:15:55.443
He refused to leave,

00:15:55.684 --> 00:15:56.724
so I had to leave.

00:15:59.505 --> 00:16:00.806
I knew my kids were safe with him.

00:16:01.506 --> 00:16:02.007
They were older,

00:16:02.607 --> 00:16:04.047
so he'd never be physical with them.

00:16:05.348 --> 00:16:05.848
Um,

00:16:05.929 --> 00:16:07.410
so it was their home,

00:16:08.311 --> 00:16:08.811
so

00:16:08.872 --> 00:16:11.294
I left and left them with him.

00:16:13.056 --> 00:16:13.556
Um,

00:16:14.318 --> 00:16:16.280
which in hindsight I wish I'd never done.

00:16:18.182 --> 00:16:19.203
That's my biggest regret.

00:16:23.171 --> 00:16:26.735
My bond with my girls is gone.

00:16:35.206 --> 00:16:36.347
We're getting it back slowly,

00:16:37.348 --> 00:16:38.169
but it's not the same.

00:16:44.231 --> 00:16:46.312
I never really knew my daughters at all.

00:16:47.492 --> 00:16:48.572
I had a great big shed,

00:16:49.653 --> 00:16:50.573
bar,
all that stuff,

00:16:50.613 --> 00:16:51.813
had all the good stuff in there.

00:16:52.353 --> 00:16:55.714
I used to drink a lot and that was my life.

00:16:56.415 --> 00:16:56.955
My trucks,

00:16:57.815 --> 00:16:58.275
my shed,

00:16:58.275 --> 00:16:58.775
my mates.

00:16:59.195 --> 00:16:59.695
And

00:17:01.896 --> 00:17:03.397
I didn't really pay any attention to

00:17:04.057 --> 00:17:05.297
Sue or what was wrong with her.

00:17:05.337 --> 00:17:06.998
I just sort of took the approach,

00:17:07.058 --> 00:17:09.318
the old-style approach and hardened up,

00:17:09.538 --> 00:17:10.038
you know.

00:17:13.251 --> 00:17:18.315
And I come to meet Dave because she'd left me and I was fairly distraught.

00:17:47.635 --> 00:17:48.796
I'll just make some sandwiches,

00:17:48.836 --> 00:17:49.656
yeah?
You happy with that?

00:17:50.597 --> 00:17:51.497
Yep.
I've got group tonight,

00:17:51.498 --> 00:17:56.060
you know that,

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:58.301
don't you?
Sasko's done a lot of work prior to coming to us.

00:17:59.121 --> 00:18:02.263
He's very open about wanting to work on himself,

00:18:03.363 --> 00:18:07.566
but has never been able to get tools or skills to change.

00:18:11.623 --> 00:18:14.507
He wants to be this father figure for his children,

00:18:14.567 --> 00:18:15.909
that is loving,

00:18:15.989 --> 00:18:16.570
supportive,

00:18:16.690 --> 00:18:17.251
underneath him.

00:18:18.793 --> 00:18:19.674
We're challenging him.

00:18:20.174 --> 00:18:21.656
I think that's been good for Sasko.

00:18:25.742 --> 00:18:26.242
Alrighty.

00:18:28.439 --> 00:18:28.780
Alright,

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:29.840
let's get the show on the road.

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:32.060
What's been happening over the week?

00:18:33.201 --> 00:18:33.881
On Saturday,

00:18:34.041 --> 00:18:37.062
my boss unleashed his anger to me.

00:18:37.063 --> 00:18:37.563
Like,

00:18:38.023 --> 00:18:40.204
he was screaming full on at me.

00:18:40.924 --> 00:18:42.024
And I had no idea what.

00:18:43.025 --> 00:18:44.045
He's asked me to leave.

00:18:44.745 --> 00:18:47.346
But I spent a lot of the day thinking,

00:18:47.927 --> 00:18:48.427
could...

00:18:49.887 --> 00:18:54.070
I have done something differently to achieve a different outcome.

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:56.991
I was playing different scenarios over and over and over again.

00:18:57.252 --> 00:18:59.273
I was really getting myself worked up.

00:18:59.673 --> 00:19:00.814
And how did that make you feel?

00:19:01.254 --> 00:19:01.754
Oh,

00:19:02.555 --> 00:19:03.055
helpless.

00:19:03.295 --> 00:19:03.796
Helpless.

00:19:03.896 --> 00:19:04.516
Fearful,

00:19:04.876 --> 00:19:05.717
embarrassed,

00:19:06.437 --> 00:19:06.938
lost,

00:19:07.318 --> 00:19:08.238
confused,

00:19:09.319 --> 00:19:10.059
belittled.

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:11.260
All those feelings.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:12.601
Phenomenal amount of feelings.

00:19:13.021 --> 00:19:14.842
So you took it on?

00:19:15.891 --> 00:19:17.212
I was trying to work out what was going on.

00:19:17.572 --> 00:19:19.413
The power and control was all in his court.

00:19:20.153 --> 00:19:22.915
It sounds like how he's been treated is probably how

00:19:23.795 --> 00:19:24.756
I've treated my wife.

00:19:24.996 --> 00:19:27.717
It sounds like the universe is giving you a taste of your own medicine.

00:19:28.378 --> 00:19:28.858
You know,

00:19:28.858 --> 00:19:30.559
just as Oscar was saying that,

00:19:30.579 --> 00:19:34.101
I haven't reflected on how my partner feels when I unleash.

00:19:35.362 --> 00:19:37.543
Now imagine if that happens all the time,

00:19:38.123 --> 00:19:40.344
whether it's once a day or once a week or once a month.

00:19:43.566 --> 00:19:44.086
You carry it.

00:19:55.243 --> 00:19:59.104
We met at the front of taxis in 2005 on the

00:19:59.985 --> 00:20:05.467
2nd of May and we fell in love instantly.

00:20:05.927 --> 00:20:07.808
It was about 7 o'clock that night.

00:20:08.428 --> 00:20:10.169
I said would you like to go out to dinner and she said no.

00:20:10.229 --> 00:20:10.729
said yes.

00:20:11.069 --> 00:20:17.553
I was so hungry that I had entremains and dessert where Susan had one meal.

00:20:18.433 --> 00:20:21.595
And so the funny thing about that is she thought I was a great listener,

00:20:21.875 --> 00:20:22.836
but I was eating.

00:20:22.837 --> 00:20:23.436
He was just eating.

00:20:23.456 --> 00:20:25.397
I was just eating and Susan was talking.

00:20:26.317 --> 00:20:27.058
And we got married

00:20:27.558 --> 00:20:28.478
12 months after that.

00:20:29.559 --> 00:20:30.600
We spent 12 months,

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:31.661
you know,
having fun.

00:20:31.661 --> 00:20:34.221
We went on a three week honeymoon and then,

00:20:34.381 --> 00:20:37.183
you know,
we got pregnant and then we moved out of home.

00:20:39.371 --> 00:20:41.292
November of 2011,

00:20:41.672 --> 00:20:42.933
I was really angry.

00:20:43.573 --> 00:20:44.773
We were out the back door.

00:20:45.333 --> 00:20:47.794
I started screaming and yelling and I head-butted the door,

00:20:48.855 --> 00:20:49.295
like,

00:20:49.295 --> 00:20:50.015
really hard,

00:20:50.135 --> 00:20:51.836
and I head-butted it again and again.

00:20:52.036 --> 00:20:53.037
Susan was up on the step.

00:20:53.077 --> 00:20:55.518
I've looked up and she's horrified.

00:20:55.558 --> 00:20:57.699
She was in shock and she said,

00:20:58.199 --> 00:20:59.159
I'm scared of you.

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:07.923
And that was the most painful thing that I've ever heard.

00:21:09.851 --> 00:21:10.331
Come at us,

00:21:10.331 --> 00:21:11.371
who's out of the bath?

00:21:13.972 --> 00:21:15.193
He's someone that I love,

00:21:16.013 --> 00:21:17.693
telling me that they're scared of me.

00:21:19.294 --> 00:21:24.216
There was a time where my son was not really putting his pyjamas on,

00:21:24.217 --> 00:21:25.216
he was playing around.

00:21:25.556 --> 00:21:27.577
He could pick up that his dad's really angry,

00:21:27.817 --> 00:21:28.817
so he got up and...

00:21:28.857 --> 00:21:29.877
and he went straight in the bed.

00:21:30.537 --> 00:21:31.378
And he said,

00:21:31.458 --> 00:21:31.778
OK,

00:21:31.778 --> 00:21:32.178
Sashko,

00:21:32.178 --> 00:21:33.798
we're going to do it over and over again.

00:21:33.878 --> 00:21:35.739
Get out of the bed and do it again.

00:21:36.139 --> 00:21:36.959
Get out of the bed,

00:21:37.019 --> 00:21:37.679
do it again.

00:21:37.779 --> 00:21:39.320
So it was yelling and yelling.

00:21:39.680 --> 00:21:42.300
And Sashko would curl up in a fetal position,

00:21:43.180 --> 00:21:43.680
my son,

00:21:44.241 --> 00:21:46.081
and he would just be shaking the whole time.

00:21:47.822 --> 00:21:50.162
His strength becomes tenfold.

00:21:50.482 --> 00:21:51.442
I can't stop him.

00:21:51.582 --> 00:21:52.903
He'll push me out of the way.

00:21:54.987 --> 00:22:01.453
And he will harm the children in my opinion.

00:22:01.454 --> 00:22:03.735
When I was a child when my dad got angry,

00:22:04.455 --> 00:22:11.441
I remember feeling scared and I remember as a child thinking I don't want to do this.

00:22:11.701 --> 00:22:13.263
If I have kids I'm not going to do this.

00:22:15.364 --> 00:22:20.349
Here I am trying to create a beautiful family and everyone's scared of me.

00:22:33.657 --> 00:22:37.141
Susannah's engaged in the women's program and seeking support too,

00:22:37.382 --> 00:22:37.882
so

00:22:39.124 --> 00:22:44.009
I really hope she embraces it and he continues to do the work he does.

00:22:51.751 --> 00:22:54.293
How many women here have felt like they're going crazy?

00:22:54.733 --> 00:22:56.274
Just put up your hand if you felt.

00:22:57.775 --> 00:23:00.697
It's really common that you take responsibility,

00:23:00.737 --> 00:23:05.059
you don't know what's real anymore and you feel like you're going absolutely crazy.

00:23:06.060 --> 00:23:06.900
There is shame,

00:23:06.920 --> 00:23:09.342
there is embarrassment where you just think to yourself,

00:23:09.422 --> 00:23:10.362
why has this happened?

00:23:10.643 --> 00:23:11.403
Did I do it?

00:23:11.483 --> 00:23:12.344
Is it my fault?

00:23:12.744 --> 00:23:14.885
Is it something that I triggered?

00:23:15.045 --> 00:23:16.806
I should have been a better wife,

00:23:16.807 --> 00:23:17.847
I should have cleaned better,

00:23:17.907 --> 00:23:19.068
I should have ironed better,

00:23:19.208 --> 00:23:20.429
I should have done all these things.

00:23:20.549 --> 00:23:20.909
So...

00:23:20.909 --> 00:23:21.789
all these pressures,

00:23:22.229 --> 00:23:26.190
you start clearing those files in your brain and think,

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:26.610
hang on,

00:23:26.610 --> 00:23:27.110
it's not me.

00:23:28.271 --> 00:23:33.952
It's a situation that he did when he was angry and it's the decision he made straight after.

00:23:34.292 --> 00:23:36.772
I feel like this group is like open heart surgery.

00:23:37.292 --> 00:23:39.293
And then you just feel relieved when you walk out.

00:23:39.294 --> 00:23:39.933
You feel like,

00:23:40.013 --> 00:23:41.773
oh,
there's that support structure.

00:23:41.774 --> 00:23:42.534
Yeah.

00:23:43.414 --> 00:23:48.735
So what this has also brought me is strength and independence.

00:23:51.271 --> 00:23:51.731
For women,

00:23:51.731 --> 00:23:55.793
it's not making them accountable or responsible for the men's behaviour,

00:23:56.754 --> 00:24:02.957
but it's making them responsible for their own choices in responding to that behaviour.

00:24:03.478 --> 00:24:07.060
So it's about educating them with what abuse is,

00:24:07.380 --> 00:24:09.661
the patterns that they're part of,

00:24:10.261 --> 00:24:12.222
and giving them tools to do it differently.

00:24:16.703 --> 00:24:19.785
I've personally experienced all forms of abuse and

00:24:20.465 --> 00:24:23.287
I've witnessed change in my own family.

00:24:25.428 --> 00:24:27.869
My abuse started through my childhood.

00:24:28.710 --> 00:24:30.471
I was sexually abused by my father.

00:24:31.551 --> 00:24:33.613
There was a lot of other subtle abuses.

00:24:33.693 --> 00:24:42.257
There was a lot of manipulation and control and a lot of stuff that wasn't obvious and that had a huge impact on who I was.

00:24:43.198 --> 00:24:44.439
I did a women's program.

00:24:46.159 --> 00:24:48.601
back then and that made a huge difference.

00:24:50.303 --> 00:24:51.183
In the men's program,

00:24:51.504 --> 00:24:53.706
I'm the voice of the women and the children.

00:24:54.586 --> 00:24:58.410
I'm a reminder for them that this has an impact.

00:25:01.052 --> 00:25:01.652
Hey fellas.

00:25:03.374 --> 00:25:05.876
I wanted just to do a debrief after last week.

00:25:07.137 --> 00:25:08.558
What's been going on for you since then?

00:25:13.507 --> 00:25:14.007
What's the matter,

00:25:14.028 --> 00:25:14.369
Justin?

00:25:14.369 --> 00:25:15.069
You just shifted.

00:25:15.549 --> 00:25:16.049
Well,

00:25:16.670 --> 00:25:17.751
sometimes it's a little hard.

00:25:17.752 --> 00:25:19.232
I don't know.

00:25:20.574 --> 00:25:23.116
When we're talking about putting it in a scenario,

00:25:23.356 --> 00:25:28.041
it all makes it sound like it's easy and we've got all the time in the world to be able to do that.

00:25:29.342 --> 00:25:34.386
What I find with men is I'll get the sceptic that'll come along who sits there and goes,

00:25:34.466 --> 00:25:35.708
why should I look at change?

00:25:35.748 --> 00:25:38.530
Why should I bother with these ideas that we talk about?

00:25:39.411 --> 00:25:43.679
One of the biggest things is sometimes wanting to let go of power and control.

00:25:44.140 --> 00:25:47.306
And some men just won't look at letting that go.

00:25:47.307 --> 00:25:49.150
I'll say to them that by holding on to that,

00:25:49.230 --> 00:25:50.993
then you're wanting to be abusive.

00:25:52.186 --> 00:25:54.067
So we're going to have a snapshot.

00:25:54.828 --> 00:25:55.828
You're on the job site.

00:25:56.630 --> 00:25:58.351
Alright,
so we've got a tree that's just fallen,

00:25:58.530 --> 00:25:59.351
pipe's broken,

00:25:59.411 --> 00:26:00.451
water's pouring everywhere.

00:26:00.892 --> 00:26:03.192
We've had a bit of stress with this client prior to this.

00:26:03.673 --> 00:26:07.576
Let's hear all the thoughts that are going through your head while all this is happening.

00:26:08.776 --> 00:26:14.539
I didn't need her and her shit on my job.

00:26:14.640 --> 00:26:16.961
So what's going through your head as you hear her talking?

00:26:17.060 --> 00:26:17.560
Fuck off,

00:26:17.662 --> 00:26:18.162
bitch.

00:26:20.671 --> 00:26:24.173
Do you reckon referring to her as a bitch is going to help this situation?

00:26:24.994 --> 00:26:25.754
Is that positive?

00:26:27.296 --> 00:26:28.136
What else we thinking?

00:26:29.177 --> 00:26:30.097
What's left to fuck off?

00:26:30.177 --> 00:26:31.198
She's still there talking.

00:26:32.799 --> 00:26:34.260
What are your ears fucking painted on?

00:26:34.261 --> 00:26:38.704
What did I just tell you woman?

00:26:38.705 --> 00:26:40.645
That she made a whole heap of fuss about nothing.

00:26:43.179 --> 00:26:43.499
You know,

00:26:43.499 --> 00:26:43.819
for me,

00:26:43.819 --> 00:26:44.600
if you said,

00:26:44.660 --> 00:26:45.160
look,

00:26:45.661 --> 00:26:46.681
this is an accident,

00:26:47.122 --> 00:26:49.423
but rest assured that this will be fixed.

00:26:49.424 --> 00:26:50.504
It's not difficult to fix.

00:26:51.365 --> 00:26:52.565
I give you that guarantee.

00:26:52.986 --> 00:26:53.666
Excuse me,

00:26:53.766 --> 00:26:58.810
I don't have the vocab skills in the heat of the moment at the end of the day.

00:26:59.470 --> 00:27:01.491
Yeah,
and I guess that's why we're doing this.

00:27:01.852 --> 00:27:06.995
How do we now throw that switch and start thinking the positives about all this?

00:27:07.175 --> 00:27:08.176
What can we be thinking?

00:27:09.717 --> 00:27:10.958
Don't know what you want me to say,

00:27:11.018 --> 00:27:11.518
Dave.

00:27:13.278 --> 00:27:13.778
Don't worry,

00:27:13.819 --> 00:27:16.420
we'll leave it there.

00:27:16.421 --> 00:27:16.921
Alrighty.

00:27:17.880 --> 00:27:18.380
Um,

00:27:19.001 --> 00:27:19.801
have a seat.

00:27:20.021 --> 00:27:21.621
We'll do this another time.

00:27:21.622 --> 00:27:22.122
Hey,

00:27:27.483 --> 00:27:27.983
Justin.

00:27:28.884 --> 00:27:30.244
Can I just have a quick word to you,

00:27:30.264 --> 00:27:33.725
please?

00:27:33.726 --> 00:27:35.285
How much did you have to drink before tonight?

00:27:36.006 --> 00:27:36.786
Two cans,

00:27:36.906 --> 00:27:37.406
Dave.

00:27:37.726 --> 00:27:38.666
I can smell it on you,

00:27:38.926 --> 00:27:40.027
and that's what I'm worried about.

00:27:42.054 --> 00:27:42.895
It's a roadblock.

00:27:43.556 --> 00:27:46.778
One minute I see you make this really positive shift,

00:27:47.158 --> 00:27:47.999
and then tonight,

00:27:48.419 --> 00:27:49.740
it's almost chalk and cheese.

00:27:51.641 --> 00:27:54.923
She could be and tell that I'm the bad guy,

00:27:54.924 --> 00:28:03.910
and I've got to fucking empathise with everyone that doesn't give a fuck about me or my job or the pressures on my life.

00:28:03.951 --> 00:28:05.731
Having a couple under your belt's not going to help.

00:28:07.452 --> 00:28:09.034
It's like pouring petrol on the fire.

00:28:11.302 --> 00:28:12.844
Especially if we're going through build-ups,

00:28:12.845 --> 00:28:14.263
especially if we're being challenged,

00:28:17.865 --> 00:28:19.046
it just worries me about him.

00:28:30.030 --> 00:28:31.350
He's certainly in a bad place.

00:28:32.192 --> 00:28:34.613
Hopefully we can just hold on to him and keep him engaged.

00:28:35.812 --> 00:28:37.953
The damage at home is severe.

00:28:39.375 --> 00:28:39.875
He...

00:28:40.502 --> 00:28:41.623
He doesn't have the answers,

00:28:41.624 --> 00:28:42.783
he doesn't have the tools.

00:28:44.223 --> 00:28:46.365
It's just got to a point where it's destroyed the family.

00:28:50.465 --> 00:28:52.646
The work we do is really challenging.

00:28:53.067 --> 00:28:59.208
We're dealing with people's lives and the reality of what we're doing is quite...

00:28:59.210 --> 00:29:00.368
..can be quite serious.

00:29:01.529 --> 00:29:02.549
It can be life-threatening.

00:29:06.147 --> 00:29:06.928
Right at this moment,

00:29:07.168 --> 00:29:11.610
I want to focus in and support you in those really strong instincts that you had.

00:29:12.351 --> 00:29:12.851
You know,

00:29:12.871 --> 00:29:14.412
you've got previous experience,

00:29:14.652 --> 00:29:16.073
you know how this goes.

00:29:17.053 --> 00:29:19.014
You were able to make a decision on the spot.

00:29:21.175 --> 00:29:22.096
It was time to get out,

00:29:22.416 --> 00:29:22.916
now,

00:29:23.056 --> 00:29:23.418
tonight.

00:29:23.418 --> 00:29:34.123
Being stuck in the house was...

00:29:35.666 --> 00:29:36.346
Very scary.

00:29:38.327 --> 00:29:42.049
And obviously you have a child and you want to protect them.

00:29:45.192 --> 00:29:49.874
I just went on autopilot and I grabbed the girls and put them straight in the car.

00:29:52.155 --> 00:29:52.975
And I drove off,

00:29:55.817 --> 00:29:57.417
thinking that I'd never see him again.

00:30:04.626 --> 00:30:06.528
I guess it's a fear of change.

00:30:06.587 --> 00:30:10.569
It's been a particular way for so long and what will I do now?

00:30:12.892 --> 00:30:18.615
You've lost your partner in spite of the fact that he wasn't a very good partner and you've lost all the,

